5. Process and Task management commands 

tasklist-displays all running processes --tasklist
taskkill-kills all running processes --taskkill /IM notepad.exe

Two ways:

By PID (find it first with tasklist):

taskkill /PID 1234
By program name (easier):

taskkill /IM notepad.exe
Force kill (if normal doesn't work):

taskkill /F /IM notepad.exe
Kill multiple at once:

taskkill /IM notepad.exe /IM chrome.exe
Example workflow:

tasklist                    → see running programs (find PID)
taskkill /PID 5678          → kill that PID
taskkill /F /IM chrome.exe  → force close all Chrome





